{"title":"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Patty has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> coins consisting of nickels and dimes. If her nickels were dimes and her dimes were nickels, she would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa94edfb9739dcc66dad90f7dd5c148f44a57e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cents more. How much are her coins worth?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/038e8ec43e6e41e81d9bb1b08d6833a1a8541ec4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\textdollar 1.15\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\textdollar 1.20\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\textdollar 1.25\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\textdollar 1.30\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\textdollar 1.35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"510\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>She has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> nickels and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/9/739219caa2ffe04a85e088df26b02c511c07dbc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=20-n$\" width=\"84\" height=\"12\" /> dimes. Their total cost is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/3/3b3effa197a78174c75caa7470ae3a1cf1e9ea7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5n+10d=5n+10(20-n)=200-5n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"313\" height=\"18\" /> cents. If the dimes were nickels and vice versa, she would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/0/5305714a6a75e62783460ce0807b41eee22c5a66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10n+5d=10n+5(20-n)=100+5n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"313\" height=\"18\" /> cents. This value should be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa94edfb9739dcc66dad90f7dd5c148f44a57e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cents more than the previous one. We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/a/49a6cb10efe07e62cd6e9baef862efc3636076a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200-5n+70=100+5n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"203\" height=\"14\" />, which solves to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e5a50f89eb87941facbb1e7b1ae91777fa10f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" />. Her coins are worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/d/5dd15377a209c0ec3848a878049a12bc5f4e90e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200-5n=\\boxed{\\mathrm{(A)\\ }\\textdollar1.15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"180\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Changing a nickel into a dime increases the sum by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cents, and changing a dime into a nickel decreases it by the same amount. As the sum increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa94edfb9739dcc66dad90f7dd5c148f44a57e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cents, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/2/d722265bd4cc8aa0b4481602785bb54b7b6678b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70/5=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> more nickels than dimes. As the total count is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, this means that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> nickels and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dimes, which is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/d/88d365fe5ac3aee8a02f1d80edcd316a1b1d8da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(A)\\ }\\textdollar1.15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"86\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B\">2004 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/i